   "subject": "Re: using Lavaan to test moderation effect",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Mikko, Alex, thank you both very much!<div><br></div><div>Now I can run the model in Mplus using xwith.</div><div><br></div><div>And I think this question and answer is relevant to mine.</div><div><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/lavaan/interaction%7Csort:date/lavaan/Zt7c8fsbFYc/ptd0YfMpCgAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/lavaan/interaction%257Csort:date/lavaan/Zt7c8fsbFYc/ptd0YfMpCgAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425940458000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3WsNIb9SCuwZbQ6fp1MA-b\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/lavaan/interaction|sort:date/lavaan/Zt7c8fsbFYc/ptd0YfMpCgAJ</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>It seems testing interaction which involves latent variable is not yet that straight forward in Lavaan, i.e. cannot be done by one operator. (And it seems : operator is being implemented for next version of Lavaan)</div><div><br></div><div>In my case it involves a first order latent variable, and a second order reflective latent variable.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m not familiar with LMS, but hope it can do this. Again, many thanks! </div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
